---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { DOCS } from '../lib/site';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../lib/jsonld';
---

<Base
  title="About: an Unofficial Jev Community Site"
  description="usejev.dev is an unofficial, community-run catalog of Jev use cases. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by TypeSafe AI in any way."
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbs([{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About', path: '/about/' }])]}
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>About usejev.dev</h1>
    <div class="note">
      <p>
        <strong>This is an unofficial, community site. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by TypeSafe
        AI.</strong> "Jev" and "TypeSafe" are names of their owner and are used here only to describe the product the
        examples are written for.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      A catalog of practical patterns for <a href={DOCS.vendor}>Jev</a>, the System One model that TypeSafe AI opened
      for early access on September 15, 2026
      (<a href={DOCS.launchPost}>launch announcement</a>). Each <a href="/use-cases/">use case</a> shows a question
      design, Python and TypeScript code, decision logic, and a cost estimate.
    </p>

    <h2>How the content is checked</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Code samples use only endpoints, fields, and SDK methods documented in the
        <a href={DOCS.api}>HTTP API reference</a>, the <a href={DOCS.python}>Python SDK docs</a>, and the
        <a href={DOCS.javascript}>JavaScript SDK docs</a>. Anything that could not be verified is labelled
        "illustrative" in the sample.
      </li>
      <li>
        Example responses are illustrative. They show the documented response shape with made-up probabilities, not
        measured output. There are no benchmarks, testimonials, or quotes on this site.
      </li>
      <li>
        Prices and limits are taken from the <a href={DOCS.models}>official models page</a> and can change. Check the
        source before you budget.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Official sources</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={DOCS.vendor}>TypeSafe AI website</a></li>
      <li><a href={DOCS.home}>Official TypeSafe documentation</a></li>
      <li><a href={DOCS.api}>HTTP API reference</a></li>
      <li><a href={DOCS.confidence}>Official confidence guide</a></li>
      <li><a href={DOCS.jaggedness}>Known limitations of jev-1.13</a></li>
      <li><a href={DOCS.launchPost}>Launch post: Introducing System One Models and Jev</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      This site uses Yandex.Metrika to count visits and see which pages are useful, including click maps and
      anonymized session replays. Text typed into the submission form is not recorded. There are no ads and no
      data is sold.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If a sample is out of date or a claim is wrong, open an issue or pull request on the site's repository. Accuracy
      matters more here than coverage.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
